## The COFF flavor still dispatches as before (ImplementationPlan.md 5.9.1,
## M13; recon p2/lld-flavor.md 1.3), the companion of dispatch.test, which
## checks msil-ld and the other flavors. lld-link and 'lld -flavor link' reach
## the COFF flavor, which still misses only inputs when given /machine:x64, a
## COFF option that the GNU flavor and msil-ld read as an input file. Its
## --version text cannot show it, because lld-link and msil-ld print the same
## line. The -flavor form names the program 'lld'.
##
## The COFF flavor reports 'no input files' through Fatal()
## (lld/COFF/Driver.cpp). With LLD_IN_TEST=2 (lit's RUN_LLD_MAIN_TWICE), lld
## silences the output of the first of its two runs and Fatal() exits from
## that run (lld/tools/lld/lld.cpp), so nothing is printed. That is upstream
## behaviour, so this test is unsupported in that mode, as
## lld/test/ELF/lto/cache-warnings.ll is; dispatch.test keeps every other
## flavor and runs in both modes.

# UNSUPPORTED: main-run-twice

# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not=error: --implicit-check-not=warning:

# RUN: not lld-link 2>&1 | %{fc} --check-prefix=COFF -DNAME=lld-link
# RUN: not lld-link /machine:x64 2>&1 | %{fc} --check-prefix=COFF -DNAME=lld-link
# RUN: not %lld_exe -flavor link 2>&1 | %{fc} --check-prefix=COFF -DNAME=lld
# RUN: not %lld_exe -flavor link /machine:x64 2>&1 | %{fc} --check-prefix=COFF -DNAME=lld

# COFF:         {{^}}[[NAME]]: error: no input files{{$}}
